# Careful mode

Apply extra scrutiny to destructive operations: recursive deletion, database drops/truncation, history rewriting, work loss and production changes. Verify the resolved target, current state, task authorization and recovery path before execution. Use the existing authorization when it covers the exact operation; ask only when scope or destructive consequences remain unresolved.

This is advisory guidance in Codex and DevSpace. It does not install a sandbox or a command interceptor. Some other hosts support the hook metadata in this template; claim enforcement only after verifying that the host registered the hook and the relevant tool is actually covered. A pattern list is not complete protection, and a directory named `build` or `cache` is not automatically safe to delete.

State that careful review is active as an agent practice, not that every command is mechanically checked. Honor the user's request to end the practice; do not alter independent host safety controls.
